1. McCabe Cyclomatic Complexity (v(g)): Captures decision-making paths; higher values are associated with defect-prone logic.
2. McCabe Essential Complexity (ev(g)): Measures structuredness; deviations from essential complexity can indicate code quality issues.
3. McCabe Design Complexity (iv(g)): Reflects module interaction complexity; intricate designs are often error-prone.
4. Lines of Code (loc): Indicates code size; larger modules are typically more defect-prone.
5. Halstead Volume (v): Proxy for cognitive complexity; high values suggest understanding difficulties associated with defects.
6. Halstead Difficulty (d): Reflects complexity in coding effort; higher difficulty often correlates with defects.
7. Halstead Effort (e): Represents effort invested; excessive effort may indicate latent defects.
8. Branch Count (branchCount): Represents flow graph branching; linked to testing effort and defect likelihood.

