   df['normalized_effort'] = df['e'] / df['e'].max()
   

2. Complexity per Size (v(g) / v): Cyclomatic complexity normalized by Halstead volume.
   python
   df['complexity_per_size'] = df['v(g)'] / (df['v'] + 1)
   

3. Halstead Efficiency (i / e): Ratio of intelligence to effort, reflecting logical efficiency.
   python
   df['halstead_efficiency'] = df['i'] / (df['e'] + 1)
   

4. Interaction between Cyclomatic Complexity and Branching Density (v(g) * branchCount): Amplifies intricate logic captured in modules.
   python
   df['cyclomatic_branch_interaction'] = df['v(g)'] * df['branchCount']
   

5. Log Volume (log(v + 1)): Log transformation of Halstead volume for smoother scaling and outlier management.
   python
   df['log_volume'] = np.log(df['v'] + 1)
   

6. Mean Complexity per Line (v(g) * l / loc): Combines cyclomatic complexity and length relative to size.
   python
   df['mean_complexity_per_line'] = (df['v(g)'] * df['l']) / (df['loc'] + 1)
   

7. Cognitive Complexity Index (branchCount * v_g_per_loc): Measures the intensity of the branching and complexity relative to size.  
   python
   df['cognitive_complexity'] = df['branchCount'] * df['v_g_per_loc']
   

